; addline_sample_leaves_domain: ADDLINE is checked on its result.
;
; The delta here is 1, which is a perfectly good binary value; the sum is 2,
; which is not. A guard that checked the operand instead of the result would
; accept this program and leave the sample holding 2, which is the whole
; failure the check exists to prevent.
;
; Paired with addline_sample_returns_to_domain, which moves by -1 from the
; same state and must succeed. A guard that rejected negative deltas, or one
; that checked the delta against the domain, would pass one and fail the
; other.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; binary sample, domain {0, 1}

PUSH 1
PUSH 1
SETLINE r0       ; values[1] = 1, the top of the domain

PUSH 1
PUSH 1
ADDLINE r0       ; 1 + 1 = 2, outside the domain
HALT
